  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study could not confirm the specific emission sources driving the observed variations in fine and coarse particle fractions.",
      "what": "This study monitored fine (PM2.5) and coarse (PM10) particulate matter alongside temperature, relative humidity, and wind speed across 14 sampling locations in Abeokuta, Nigeria. The analysis compared paved and unpaved urban corridors using statistical modeling, Air Quality Index classification, and geospatial interpolation to map concentration fields and calculate PM2.5/PM10 ratios.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that unpaved roads significantly increase coarse-mode particulate loading through mechanical resuspension, establishing a direct link between road surface type and localized air quality variations in a rapidly expanding tropical city."
    }
  },
